1
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:38,000
In 1917, in the midst of a world war, people
needed hope. They received a miracle.

2
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:10,000
Fatima is a drama film directed by Marco Pontecorvo.

3
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:42,000
In 1917, outside the parish of Fátima, Portugal, a 10-year-old girl and her two younger cousins witness multiple
visitations of the Virgin Mary, who tells them that only prayer and suffering will bring an end to World War I.

4
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:14,000
As secularist government officials and Church leaders try to force the children to recant their story, word of the sighting
spreads across the country, inspiring religious pilgrims to flock to the site in hopes of witnessing a miracle..

5
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:46,000
Professor Nichols, played by Harvey Keitel.

6
00:45:12,000 --> 00:45:18,000
Sister Lucia, played by Sônia Braga.

7
00:52:44,000 --> 00:52:50,000
Artur, played by Goran Višnjić.

8
01:00:16,000 --> 01:00:22,000
Father Ferreira, played by Joaquim de Almeida.

9
01:07:48,000 --> 01:07:54,000
Maria Rosa, played by Lúcia Moniz.

10
01:15:20,000 --> 01:15:26,000
Mary, played by Joana Ribeiro.

11
01:22:52,000 --> 01:22:58,000
Fátima is a 2020 faith-based drama film directed by Marco Pontecorvo.

12
01:30:24,000 --> 01:30:30,000
It stars Joaquim de Almeida, Goran Višnjić, Harvey Keitel, Sônia Braga,
Stephanie Gil, Alejandra Howard, Jorge Lamelas and Lúcia Moniz.

13
01:37:56,000 --> 01:38:02,000
The film, based on Our Lady of Fátima, features the original song "Gratia Plena" ("Full of
Grace"), performed by Andrea Bocelli and composed by Italian composer Paolo Buonvino.

14
01:45:28,000 --> 01:45:34,000
The tone is uplifting and emotional.
